<!-- ID: phase_review_results -->
Package reviewed: Forge Package 2.3, Research Hygiene Rule Migration.

Status: PASS.

Score: 96/100.

Legal to route Phase 3 / Package 3.1: YES.

Verified package outcomes:
- `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/quality/rules/research.py` now owns research placement and index hygiene checks.
- `SCF_NONCANONICAL_LOCATION`, `SCF_INDEX_MISSING`, `SCF_DOC_UNINDEXED`, and `SCF_INDEX_STALE` remain the warning IDs emitted by the direct research rule path.
- Direct research warnings include `source_owner: research`.
- `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/scaffold_quality.py` remains the compatibility facade and still owns changelog and release-context behavior instead of migrating it into the new research module.
- `tests/test_manage_docs_project_health_quality.py` exercises project-health compatibility and explicitly checks direct research warning owner metadata.
- `CHECKLIST.md` `p2-research-rules` proof is readable, non-truncated, and consistent with the reviewed behavior.
<!-- ID: detailed_analysis -->
Findings: none blocking.

Evidence summary:
- `research.py` builds research-only warning payloads through `_research_warning`, pulling severity and blocking from shared policies while stamping `source_owner` as `research`.
- The noncanonical, missing-index, unindexed-doc, orphaned-link, and stale-index paths are still present in the migrated rule module with the same warning codes and non-blocking medium policy inherited from `DEFAULT_WARNING_POLICIES`.
- `collect_managed_doc_quality_warnings` in `scaffold_quality.py` still gates research hygiene through `is_research_doc_target`, keeps changelog/release-context handling in the facade, and delegates only research index hygiene into the new module.
- `tests/test_manage_docs_project_health_quality.py` verifies `SCF_INDEX_MISSING` reaches project health for registered research docs, confirms direct warnings carry `source_owner == "research"`, and confirms non-research `SCF_DOC_UNINDEXED` warnings do not masquerade as research index failures.
- `CHECKLIST.md` line item `p2-research-rules` states the moved module, preserved codes, source-owner metadata, project_health coverage, and required command set without visible truncation.
- Current workspace also contains unrelated in-flight changes in `src/scribe_mcp/doc_management/runtime.py` and `tests/test_manage_docs_quality_check.py`; I treated those as adjacent dirty-tree context rather than Package 2.3 scope because they were not part of the reported Package 2.3 handoff.

Residual risk:
- `tests/doc_management/test_quality_registry.py` is still a general deterministic-order test and does not specifically assert registry registration of the research evaluator. This is a small coverage gap, not a blocker, because the direct behavioral tests and command suite already prove the migrated path in the current tree.
<!-- ID: recommendations -->
Recommendation: accept Package 2.3 and route Phase 3 / Package 3.1.

Follow-up note:
- When Phase 3 work lands, keep release-mode and changelog tests clearly separated from research hygiene proofs so later validation can attribute failures to the correct package boundary.
